module gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census



data compile_diagnostic_census_charter_note: String = "THE PROBE OBSERVATION SURFACE for the v1 compile path (roadmap node ladder-probe-corpus; gap analysis sec 12 Stage 1a). The probe corpus needs to observe WHICH judgment a synthetic source provoked, not merely that something refused: the Stage-0 receipt vocabulary gunbc.guarantee_measurement carries RefusedTyped \{diagnostic_class, count} and AcceptedCounted \{diagnostic_class, count}, and neither is inhabitable from a Bool. Before this surface the only .dag-callable v1 compile was compile_dag_rust_emit_check, which counts diagnostics passing compile_clean_diagnostic_is_hard and returns false when that count is nonzero - so class identity, severity, and every advisory were discarded inside the host. Three things that costs, each measured on the tests this corpus migrates: a probe refusing for ANY hard reason (including a typo in the probe source itself) reads as the wall firing; demoting a landed wall from blocking to advisory turns its RED silently GREEN, because the filter IS the severity predicate; and a positive control cannot state zero-diagnostics-of-ANY-severity, which is the assertion codex review 45357 added after an advisory MethodExistenceUndecided passed unnoticed as a green control. MEASUREMENT ONLY: no arm here judges acceptance. The rows carry what the compile decided, severity included AS DATA, and callers filter."

data compile_diagnostic_census_grounding_note: String = "SECTION 3 - this is a PROJECTION, not a second diagnostic vocabulary. diagnostic_class is exactly the class half of the host's compile_clean_diagnostic_histogram_key, whose total match over v1.std.core CompilerDiagnostic is the single authority for naming a variant; subject_name is that key's name half. Declaring the variants again here as a coproduct would fork the authority and drift the moment a variant lands, so the class arrives as a projected string and the compiler's own exhaustiveness is what keeps it total. blocking is likewise projected, not restated: the host reads it through the existing compile_clean_diagnostic_is_hard delegation to is_interpreter_blocking_diagnostic, so the severity POLICY has one home and this surface reports its verdict rather than re-deciding it."

data compile_diagnostic_census_path_scope_note: String = "THE ONE PATH THIS SURFACE MEASURES, stated so a receipt cannot claim coverage it does not have (DESIGN 4b: a class's rung is the MINIMUM across its in-scope paths, and citing the strongest path while another stays silent is inflation). The census compiles a synthetic single-module source through the v1 pipeline to the Rust render target - the same pipeline family compile_dag_rust_emit_check uses - WITH type_ref_hit_ne_bind_measure_active armed for that nested compile only (N1a; host bracket v1_rt::with_type_ref_hit_ne_bind_measure). That is a real path split on masked type-reference sites: census can emit blocking UnresolvedType for pool-present non-authority refs while compile_dag_rust_emit_check (measure off) stays on the production fail-open / UnlistedImportUse advisory path. Census-derived receipts must not be read as production compile-clean behavior for those positions (review 47457). In GuaranteePath axes that is subject_grain SyntheticProgram and acceptance_boundary CompileAccept. The pipeline is v1, and that is stated here as a fact about this surface rather than as a path axis: compile_mode was deleted from the path row (gunbc#7572, review 46308) because every landed control derives its pipeline from its boundary, so storing it was dual representation. If a path is ever measured under two pipelines at ONE boundary, that is the trigger returning the axis as a stored fact - not a reason to keep a copy of it here meanwhile. It observes NOTHING about the interpreter's disposition of the same program, nothing about other emission targets, and nothing about corpus-grain prevalence. A probe row keyed to a path this surface does not measure must not carry a receipt derived from it."

data compile_diagnostic_census_not_runnable_note: String = "CensusNotRunnable is a separate arm and NOT an empty row list, because an empty census is byte-identical to a clean compile (DESIGN 5: top-as-answer conflated with top-as-ignorance is the absorbing fallback). Could-not-measure must never be readable as the subject passing: the probe layer maps this arm to guarantee_measurement ProbeObservation ProbeNotRunnable, whose observed_is_verdict is false, and it can do so without guessing precisely because the separation is preserved here at the host seam rather than reconstructed downstream. An infrastructural failure of the compile itself - a harness error, an unreadable module index, a panic caught at the boundary - lands here with its cause, never as a green census."

data compile_diagnostic_census_hand_rust_dissolve_trigger: std.dissolution.DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "dissolve-on for the HAND-RUST OBSERVATION SURFACE behind this vocabulary - cli_run compile_dag_diagnostic_census (the host census fold) and v1_interpreter compile_diagnostic_census_value (the substrate projection), together with the v1.compiler.infer_method builtin_function_registry row that types it. The registry row's own trigger is its sibling's, the PrimitiveDefinition identity join; THIS row covers the Rust surface itself, which that trigger does not reach. TRIGGER, one and checkable: the roadmap row v1-zero-hand-maintained-rust, the v1-exit lane's fourth finish line. Its acceptance condition is that no hand-maintained Rust remains in the seed, so this surface is gone when that row is accepted and still owed while it is not - a state readable from the roadmap authority rather than from anyone's judgment about how far v2 has got. An earlier cut of this row offered two open-ended alternatives instead - v2 self-hosting the pipeline 'far enough' that a probe could read modeled diagnostics, or a floor-enrolled diagnostic lens subsuming the projection - and named no row; neither was evaluable, and a trigger nobody can evaluate is indistinguishable from no trigger, which is exactly the untracked-stall shape DESIGN 4b forbids (codex review 46264). EARLIER REMOVAL IS PERMITTED AND EXPECTED, but it is not the trigger: if a diagnostic lens subsumes this projection, or v2 self-hosts the pipeline far enough to read modeled diagnostics directly, this surface should go then. A scaffold may always dissolve early; what a trigger fixes is the point by which it MUST be gone, and stating the early paths as alternatives was what made the obligation unfalsifiable. It does NOT dissolve merely because the registry is replaced: the projection is the scaffold, the registry row is only its type declaration. WHY IT IS A SCAFFOLD AND NOT A PERMANENT SURFACE: everything it computes already exists inside the compiler - compile_clean_diagnostic_histogram_key names the variant and compile_clean_diagnostic_is_hard decides severity - so this adds NO judgment, only a substrate-visible projection of judgments the compiler already made. That is precisely the shape that dissolves when the substrate can read them directly. Receipt while it stands: the surface has exactly one class of consumer, the guarantee probe corpus, and its executing evidence is dag/test/claim/compile_diagnostic_census_witness_test.dag.")

data compile_diagnostic_census_hand_rust_scaffold: std.disposition.Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: std.decl_ref.DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census",
    decl_name: "compile_diagnostic_census_hand_rust_dissolve_trigger",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

type CompileDiagnosticCensusRow {
  diagnostic_class: std.types.NonEmptyStr
  subject_name: String
  blocking: Bool
  count: Int
}

type CompileDiagnosticCensus
  = CensusObserved { rows: std.types.List<CompileDiagnosticCensusRow> }
  | CensusNotRunnable { cause: std.types.NonEmptyStr }

data census_projection_note: String = "Pure reads over ROWS, never over the census. The selectors take List<CompileDiagnosticCensusRow>, so the only way to obtain rows is to MATCH the coproduct - which makes reading a row list out of a CensusNotRunnable structurally unwritable rather than warned against. An earlier cut exported census_rows(c: CompileDiagnosticCensus) answering [] on the NotRunnable arm, with a prose caution telling callers not to read a zero out of it. That was the fail-open this module exists to prevent, one layer up and in its own API: could-not-measure and observed-nothing became the same empty list at the export boundary, and a prose warning is validation standing exactly where construction was available (DESIGN 5; caught by codex review 46144). The caution deleted WITH the accessor rather than surviving beside it - a warning about a state that can no longer be written is dead text. None of these decides acceptance: blocking and advisory partition the SAME rows by the severity the host already reported, and census_total_count sums counts rather than rows so a class occurring twice is two occurrences."

fn census_blocking_rows(rows: List<CompileDiagnosticCensusRow>) -> List<CompileDiagnosticCensusRow> {
  rows |> filter(r => r.blocking)
}

fn census_advisory_rows(rows: List<CompileDiagnosticCensusRow>) -> List<CompileDiagnosticCensusRow> {
  rows |> filter(r => !r.blocking)
}

fn census_rows_of_class(rows: List<CompileDiagnosticCensusRow>, wanted: String) -> List<CompileDiagnosticCensusRow> {
  rows |> filter(r => (r.diagnostic_class as String) == wanted)
}

fn census_total_count(rows: List<CompileDiagnosticCensusRow>) -> Int {
  fold(rows, init: 0, f: (acc, r) => acc + r.count)
}
